     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to do a multivariate spatial model with about 10 variables, extended the example here( <a href=\"https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-manipula.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-manipula.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441424523000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0J0pr4Ym8RDJPytlX451H4\">https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/spde-gitbook/ch-manipula.html</a> which originally has 3 variables) but it&#39;s super slow due to too many parameters when using LMC with 10 variables. I wonder if INLA support a low rank modeling of LMC, eg, Y(.) ~ A*Z(.) + E(.), where A is 10 x 5 matrix instead of 10 x 10 ? (of course Z(.) will be a 5x1 vector then)</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
