     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks for the reply! <div><br></div><div>I tried to modify the rank of 3-likelihood model in the example to rank 2: in inla.stack(), each data list has only 2 elements, and in the final inla() model,  use <a style=\"background:0px 0px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:inherit;white-space:pre;letter-spacing:0.2px;color:rgb(65,131,196);box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold;font-size:inherit\">rep</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160);font-size:inherit\">&#39;gaussian&#39;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112);font-size:inherit\">2</span>) <span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;letter-spacing:normal;white-space:normal\">instead of</span> </a><a style=\"background:0px 0px;font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;font-size:inherit;white-space:pre;letter-spacing:0.2px;color:rgb(65,131,196);box-sizing:border-box;display:inline-block;line-height:1.25\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(0,112,32);font-weight:bold;font-size:inherit\">rep</span>(<span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,112,160);font-size:inherit\">&#39;gaussian&#39;</span>, <span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(64,160,112);font-size:inherit\">3</span>)</a>. The model will run without any error, but there&#39;s no random element output for the 3rd element (I guess INLA recognize the model as 2-variable and totally ignored the 3rd element that resembles the other.)<div><br></div><div>Is there something wrong with my modification? I wonder how to get all predictions from INLA with the low rank A matrix in LMC model.</div><div><div><br></div><div>The modified code with rank 2 model is here for your reference:<br><div><pre style=\"box-sizing:border-box;font-family:Cons